{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible","id":1101722,"title":"Is the birth rate of Garou mathematically impossible","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-08T13:43:07-07:00","id":1101722,"title":"Is the birth rate of Garou mathematically impossible","content":"Something I often wondered but did not say aloud. The birthrate of garou is mathematically impossible to sustain a viable population if only 10% of births breed properly. Otherwise the garou would be the most promiscuous creatures on Earth having many partners and keeping as many people pregnant at all times, the womenfolk would need to be barefoot and pregnant all the time. With only a 10% replacement rate they would have gone extinct back in the stone age. Are there any population statisticians to back this up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T14:33:33-07:00","id":1101739,"title":"","content":"Garou do not have to be exceptionally promiscuous if male Garou do not practice monogamy. If we assume normal human fertility, a male Garou will sire one child for every 40 unprotected sexual encounters with female humans and 50% of those children would reach puberty. The average male Garou would only have to have 1600 unprotected sexual encounters in their life to produce one female Garou child and one male child who reach puberty and experience the change (the remaining nine surviving girls will be female Kinfolk while the remaining nine surviving boys will be male Kinfolk). Before modern reproductive technologies, that could be done in five years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T14:39:40-07:00","id":1101745,"title":"","content":"In other news: water wet.<br /> <br /> The numbers for such things were just sort of made up and once they were in the books, even after people figured out they didn't add up well, they were the numbers. It's a bit of a dead horse.<br /> <br /> Though that bit of snark aside, the numbers aren't actually that bad. They don't work, but they're not as grim as you're saying either. Also the Garou are <u>supposed to be dying out</u> so the unsustainable numbers are probably the idea; even if again, they don't add up well.<br /> <br /> 10% (which isn't a set rate, but lets run with it anyway) isn't the replacement rate. The base replacement rate is the number of children that need to be born to replace the parents. In a sexually reproducing species, the lowest possible rate is an average of 2 children per female for the total global population (in a local population it can go lower via migration), however this is then modified by the mortality rate of children before they reach child rearing age. So humans living in a society with high levels of medical technology and common access to it, the replacement rate can easily be between 2 and 3, as long as most adults have children. A replacement rate of 2.1 would imply a very low child mortality rate, high fertility rates, and most women reproducing. Lots of species have very high replacement rates because they have very high pre-reproductive ability mortality rates. Salmon give birth to a lot of eggs just to maintain a population because very few of those eggs will survive to reproduce.<br /> <br /> The issue with applying population statistics to the Garou is that the Garou don't work like a species. Garou don't mate with other Garou to produce a stable population. Garou mate with kinfolk, humans, and wolves to produce both more Garou and more kin, and kin can also produce Garou without mating with a Garou.<br /> <br /> So it isn't as simple as saying a female Garou needs to give birth to at least three Garou children (figure that despite Garou health and magic, 1/3 cubs isn't going to survive the violent lives of Garou to mate), and at a 10% birth rate would then have to have thirty total children over their lives (though for lupus Garou that's not such a difficulty). You also have kin producing children in kin-kin pairings. If you assuming a 1% birth rate of Garou in kin-kin populations, 300 kin females having one child would have the same impact as one Garou female's contributions to a stable replacement rate.<br /> <br /> This becomes the crux of why the numbers don't add up well: we don't have good figures on both lupus and homid kin numbers compared to the Garou population, as well as how to judge their replacement capabilities compared to average members of wolf and human populations (do they out produce because the Garou are actively influencing this and and spiritual influence, or under produce because they're targets of the Garou's enemies?). There's a bunch of variables, and most assumptions play out poorly when crunched (mostly that way more of the human population would have to be kin then the books imply).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T15:03:06-07:00","id":1101750,"title":"","content":"If we assume 10 Human Kinfolk for every Homid Garou and 10 Wolf Kinfolk for every Lupus Garou, the population is not that high. If Garou of the Garou Nation are 1:500,000 of the global Human population, the result is 15,000 Garou members of the Garou Nation (let us say 12,000 Homid, 1500 Lupus, and 1500 Metis). That would translate to 120,000 Human Garou Kinfolk and 15,000 Wolf Garou Kinfolk, which is not that large of a population (though I tend to assume higher populations of Garou Kinfolk and lower populations of Metis).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 06-08-2017, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T15:56:59-07:00","id":1101773,"title":"","content":"The problem is mostly that those numbers of kin aren't really enough to support a population of 15,000 Garou if we assume that most female Garou don't get pregnant that many times due to all the other things they're meant to do. Your numbers make sense descriptively for how the game is written, but don't make sense from a population statistics level (unless you assume kin-kin matings produce far more Garou that the books have stated in the past).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T15:58:37-07:00","id":1101776,"title":"","content":"Basically, it's magic. The game has a very creationist style cosmology heavy on things like destiny and the like, and Garou are born sort of the same way a Slayer is &quot;chosen&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T19:09:44-07:00","id":1101830,"title":"","content":"While yes, handwaving with the spirit side of things works in general, we have things like approximate numbers of the Garou, and birth rates of Garou/Kin and how they differ depending on Garou-Garou, Garou-Kin, Garou-non-Kin, Kin-Kin, Kin-non-Kin. That books didn't just leave these as vague things to chalk up to magic. There's approximate numbers in the canon as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T20:18:25-07:00","id":1101848,"title":"","content":"Magic needs to make sense internally in the system, obeying the ligic of magic in the system, or else the suspension of disbelief suffers. Just saying that it is magic is rather lazy and excuses writers for not doing basic math. Of course, there is no real problem with the numbers, as male Garou are quite capable of hooking up with a different mate every night of the week (and twice on Sundays).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T20:33:34-07:00","id":1101851,"title":"","content":"There's a reason biological population methodologies generally ignore males: they're not the controlling factor. A male Garou might be capable to have lots and lots of reproductive sex, but actually realizing that is a separate matter. Wolf kin are only going to be receptive during their heat. Homid kin are going to be selective about mating just like humans are. Garou society also treats mating rights rather seriously, limiting options within a given territory along Tribal lines, and Garou hierarchies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T21:08:22-07:00","id":1101854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible#post1101722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I often wondered but did not say aloud. The birthrate of garou is mathematically impossible to sustain a viable population if only 10% of births breed properly. Otherwise the garou would be the most promiscuous creatures on Earth having many partners and keeping as many people pregnant at all times, the womenfolk would need to be barefoot and pregnant all the time. With only a 10% replacement rate they would have gone extinct back in the stone age. Are there any population statisticians to back this up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except you ignore the fact most Garou would be born from Kinfolk. You're basically ignoring a large portion of humanity has werewolf blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T23:21:54-07:00","id":1101869,"title":"","content":"Yeah seriously, there are much more then 10 Kinfolk per Garou because Kinfolk can produce other Kinfolk with each other at a 50 percent success rate, and with normal humans with an unspecified success rate.<br /> <br /> Its also pointed out the 10% chance to make a garou child with a Kinfolk is a modern degeneration of previous fertility rates. Its likely the 30 Percent breed true rate that the Ajaba reached through unnamed dark pacts are closer to the Original birth rate of the Fera in Olden Times.<br /> <br /> But anyways its supposed to be their numbers are dying out for a reason, so it fits. Shortly after the Red Star popping up all Garou who are destined to participate in the Apocalypse are already born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T23:28:06-07:00","id":1101871,"title":"","content":"Are you accounting for the other 9/10 children being kin who carry the recessive trait and can also have Garou children with other kin 1/10 of the time?<br /> <br /> Most Garou are children of two kinfolk, not other Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T23:37:37-07:00","id":1101874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1101854#post1101854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except you ignore the fact most Garou would be born from Kinfolk. You're basically ignoring a large portion of humanity has werewolf blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but sadly that is actually never been used in the books well. Forsaken uses it to explain that, yeah, uratha can pop out whenever and wherever. But in WtA, unless your family is closely tied to garou, generally you don't shift.<br /> <br /> Again, this is mostly the setting material flip flopping on itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T00:16:38-07:00","id":1101878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1101874#post1101874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but sadly that is actually never been used in the books well. Forsaken uses it to explain that, yeah, uratha can pop out whenever and wherever. But in WtA, unless your family is closely tied to garou, generally you don't shift.<br /> <br /> Again, this is mostly the setting material flip flopping on itself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No this happened all the time, so maybe you are just more familiar with Foresaken. These Lost Cubs are often not given Kin Fetch since Garou never knew about the Birth. The Storyteller/player guide info in several books mention it, mentioning these are often exceptionally tragic first changes since they often orphan themselves by killing one or more of their parents in their first change.<br /> <br /> Several come to mind off the top of my head. Even Heals the Past was a blond white who was the product of a long seperated Wendigo Kinfolk who was the first garou in his family in like 3 or 4 generations. In one of the revised books, book of the City or maybe book of Auspices, there was an adult (I think Middle Aged) Japanese Businessman who had his first change really late in life and in America, who was a long seperated Hakken line. Then there was the infamous Amish Get of Fenris Incident...<br /> <br /> Yeah its been consistent part of the gameline since the beginning, wasn't the Valkenburg Foundation a book specifically about such lost cubs, being found by the Wyrm tainted before other Garou and locked up in an insane asylum? Even in A World of Rage W20 we have a cub completely ignorant of Garou Culture because being born away from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T00:31:14-07:00","id":1101880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1101874#post1101874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but sadly that is actually never been used in the books well. Forsaken uses it to explain that, yeah, uratha can pop out whenever and wherever. But in WtA, unless your family is closely tied to garou, generally you don't shift.<br /> <br /> Again, this is mostly the setting material flip flopping on itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, I took it as more the fact werewolves are very incestuous and expected to breed like....well, animals. Kinfolk being used as breeding slaves is something which has been touched on many times.<br /> <br /> Albeit lightly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T01:26:41-07:00","id":1101886,"title":"","content":"Not very incestuous... just a touch inbred. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well unless you are talking about the Silver Fangs...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T05:03:03-07:00","id":1101929,"title":"","content":"The problem with normal human sexual selection is that the Garou can trump it. If the human female is straight or bi and at all receptive to sex, she will jump in the sack with a male Garou. Given the sex drive of healthy male humans before the age of 30, the male Garou would have historically had no issue with sustaining the Garou population. Now, the Silver Fangs are a different story...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T06:27:29-07:00","id":1101948,"title":"","content":"Polygyny should be extremely common among werewolves. Female kinfolk should basically be harems for male Garou. This has greater potential when it comes to wolves who can reproduce way faster than humans. Actually, make werewolves should be as promiscuous as possible, as even a child with a human woman will lead to kinfolk. It's all pretty weird if you give it too much thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T06:33:43-07:00","id":1101950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1101874#post1101874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but sadly that is actually never been used in the books well. Forsaken uses it to explain that, yeah, uratha can pop out whenever and wherever. But in WtA, unless your family is closely tied to garou, generally you don't shift.<br /> <br /> Again, this is mostly the setting material flip flopping on itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression from the books as well as my experience from gameplay is that the majority of non-SF Garou are born to Kin-Kin pairings who are not directly connected to Garou society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T07:04:45-07:00","id":1101959,"title":"","content":"Polygamy seems to be rather instinctive in humans, as we do not really mate for life, so I do not see why Garou, who have the ability to be very sexually attractive to receptive members of the opposite sex, would be any different. There really is no advantage for a male Garou to mate with female Kinfolk, as female Kinfolk have to possess Pure Breed to change the odds of reproduction, and there are a lot more female Mortals than there are female Kinfolk. Of course, if female Kinfolk outnumber male Garou by a large factor (50:1 or so), then it makes sense for male Garou to mate with female Kinfolk because there are less complications (unless they are Silver Fangs...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T07:23:28-07:00","id":1101967,"title":"","content":"A few things:<br /> <br /> 1. I don't think the Garou nation wants to encourage the conception of a large number of lost cubs. The Garou nation isn't set up to track a large number of mortal woman just in case their offspring goes though the change. There's a good chance the lost cub will breach the veil, get collected by the BSD, or just get put down rather than be found by the Garou Nation. <br /> 2. Most woman who have a one night stand use condoms. If the condoms break, they use the morning after pill. If those fail, they usually get an abortion. Even if the Male Garou is Super Sexy, it doesn't mean a child will come of the encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T07:28:05-07:00","id":1101969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1101959#post1101959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Polygamy seems to be rather instinctive in humans, as we do not really mate for life...</div> </div> </div> </div>[CITATION NEEDED]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T07:50:49-07:00","id":1101982,"title":"","content":"Most women who have one night stands with strangers don't intend to have children from those encounters. In our modern world with birth control and abortion, preventing unwanted children isn't too hard. Of course, there will be some Garou born from such encounters, which will be lost cubs and so open up another can of worms. <br /> <br /> Really though, if 1% if kinfolk's children are born Garou, then if kinfolk outnumber Garou 100-1 then the Garou themselves don't even have to give birth to or sire Garou themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T11:56:59-07:00","id":1102060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1101948#post1101948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Polygyny should be extremely common among werewolves. Female kinfolk should basically be harems for male Garou. This has greater potential when it comes to wolves who can reproduce way faster than humans. Actually, make werewolves should be as promiscuous as possible, as even a child with a human woman will lead to kinfolk. It's all pretty weird if you give it too much thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Numerous issues with this.<br /> <br /> * Garou have to raise their children to be Garou. Siring random kids will likely lead to more Black Spiral Dancers or crazy litany breaking cannibals.<br /> * Black Furies have issues with those who treat women as property.<br /> * Garou are poor as hell and mostly live off their kinfolk so treating them as property is a bad idea.<br /> * Garou probably don't actually make it that much more likely to sire werewolves than Kinfolk. The gene is there and it's always recessive. So a Kin pairing is as likely to birth it as not.<br /> * Garou don't have time to take care of harems.<br /> <br /> Ironically, Garou DO mate all the time-it's just they mate with the wives and daughters of Kin family.<br /> <br /> Which is why Kinfolk often hate Garou as much as revere them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T14:20:21-07:00","id":1102109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1101848#post1101848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saying that it is magic is rather lazy and excuses writers for not doing basic math.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you're calling me lazy? I'm unclear. In this brave new world of taking offense at everything, am I supposed to flag this is a personal attack or not?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T14:47:03-07:00","id":1102116,"title":"","content":"No, I am not saying that. It is just that saying that it is magic is a lazy argument by writers because magic should always follow intrinsic logic by the definitions of the setting. If it does not, the suspension of disbelief necessary to accept the setting is lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T14:53:15-07:00","id":1102118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1101959#post1101959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Polygamy seems to be rather instinctive in humans, as we do not really mate for life, so I do not see why Garou, who have the ability to be very sexually attractive to receptive members of the opposite sex, would be any different. There really is no advantage for a male Garou to mate with female Kinfolk, as female Kinfolk have to possess Pure Breed to change the odds of reproduction, and there are a lot more female Mortals than there are female Kinfolk. Of course, if female Kinfolk outnumber male Garou by a large factor (50:1 or so), then it makes sense for male Garou to mate with female Kinfolk because there are less complications (unless they are Silver Fangs...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, you're mixing up some commodities.<br /> <br /> Humans are not MONOGAMOUS but they're not polygamous because that requires us to marry and many cultures don't practice that as well as severely censure it.<br /> <br /> They're polyAMOROUS.<br /> <br /> *pendantic werewolf here*<br /> <br /> <b>How CT Phipps handles it</b><br /> <br /> In my game, the Garou Nation has a dismissive attitude to Kinfolk in general with both sexes expected to turn out as many Garou as possible. They're equivalent to religions which don't practice birth control and emphasize large families--because they <i>are</i> a religion which does that. However, the issue is complicated because it's a SECRET religion. Garou kinfolk have to hide their faith or emphasize it under other religions. They tend to marry in-between existing kinfolk families and oftentimes they are expected to breed with existing Garou. While this, biologically, sounds like it would favor Garou men over Garou women (and does), plenty of Garou women give birth at least once or twice during their lives before handing their children over to Kinfolk families.<br /> <br /> Few Garou also &quot;marry&quot; because it's basically like the worst of military lives with Garou expected fight continuously until they die in the War against the WyrmTM. The ones who live at Septs and have a permanent positition there as their guardians have more options to have &quot;families&quot; but it's still a violent life where Garou who live to old age being very rare. The issue of real-life genetics is also it's a science is also complicated by the fact what people thought they knew about genetics is a lot more different than reality. In real life, there's a lot more adultery and people raising other people's children than people ever thought. Mostly because women have been a lot more active about rebelling against enforced marriages than you ever think.<br /> <br /> Genetics-wise, Kinfolk tend to carry the genes from not only an immediate Garou parent but parents from generations past and any partners they have are likely to be Kinfolk themselves. But when they pass on their genes to non-Kinfolk, that gene can lay dormant for generations before popping up. So yeah, I do think 100:1 Kinfolk per Garou sounds about right. For the most part, I think Kinfolk probably control other Kinfolk as they're the people who handle the raising of children, the arranged marriages, the finances, and so on.<br /> <br /> If this sounds like it could be rife with abuse, fundamentalism, and worse then you're right, it is. The Garou have a lot of ugliness to their culture which it's up to players to rebel against or reform because Garou history is human history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T15:06:53-07:00","id":1102122,"title":"","content":"I generally have the Garou being more respectful and more responsive to their Kinfolk. They encourage Kinfolk to develop their talents (magical or mundane) and depend on them for everyday services. Of course, Kinfolk outnumber Garou 100:1 in my games, so the Garou cannot really afford to alienate their Kinfolk since their Kinfolk raise the vast majority of the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T15:49:23-07:00","id":1102130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1102060#post1102060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Numerous issues with this.<br /> <br /> * Garou have to raise their children to be Garou. Siring random kids will likely lead to more Black Spiral Dancers or crazy litany breaking cannibals.<br /> * Black Furies have issues with those who treat women as property.<br /> * Garou are poor as hell and mostly live off their kinfolk so treating them as property is a bad idea.<br /> * Garou probably don't actually make it that much more likely to sire werewolves than Kinfolk. The gene is there and it's always recessive. So a Kin pairing is as likely to birth it as not.<br /> * Garou don't have time to take care of harems.<br /> <br /> Ironically, Garou DO mate all the time-it's just they mate with the wives and daughters of Kin family.<br /> <br /> Which is why Kinfolk often hate Garou as much as revere them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I shouldn't have used the word harem, because that implies that the Garou act as true husbands and support their wives. More likely is that the kinfolk marry each other but that Garou impregnate the female kinfolk instead of their husbands or lovers. Maybe like Prima Nocte, where nobles had sex with newly wedded women instead if their husbands. Those male kinfolk need to be cuckholds in a sense, they need to stick around to raise the children of the Garou and female kinfolk.<br /> <br /> This arrangement obviously won't endear the werewolves to their kinfolk. <br /> <br /> I thought that there was a 10% chance of a Garou born when a Garou mates with kinfolk as opposed to kinfolk having children with each other.<br /> <br /> I guess a question is how far Garou are willing to go when it comes to exploiting their kinfolk. I've imagined that it is pretty far in the cases of the most calloused werewolves anyway. <br /> <br /> As Aya Tari says, kinfolk will raise most Garou, so maybe in general the Garou will have too much respect for the family who raised them to mistreat kinfolk too badly. That raises an interesting issue - is Garou culture essentially kinfolk culture, as it is the kinfolk who are bearing and raising the children and who actually transmit culture rather than Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T16:02:08-07:00","id":1102132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1102060#post1102060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The gene is there and it's always recessive. So a Kin pairing is as likely to birth it as not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a gene. No matter how much KABA went backsliding on a rocket sled, it simply just doesn't make sense in terms of polypeptide chains. Hence DNA's terminal confusion at their results.<br /> <br /> (Also, it being recessive double doesn't make sense, because recessive traits often get to be the way they are because production of a polypeptide chain either got turned off completely or ended up as nonfunctional. Also, it keeps things too basic in an explanation of genetics, since it ignores complex traits, penetrance, and other factors not covered in introductory life science sections.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-09-2017, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T16:02:37-07:00","id":1102133,"title":"","content":"In the case where Kinfolk raise most of the Garou (and Kinfolk) children, I imagine that Garou society would have three levels. The first level would be the society seen by outsiders and Mortal children born of Kinfolk-Kinfolk pairings. The second level would be the society known to mundane Kinfolk. The third level would be the society known to magically gifted Kinfolk and the Garou. In any case, the Kinfolk would probably be the keepers of the traditions, as the Garou would be too busy with hunting down the minions of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> In the first case, the Veil is protected from Mortals (Mortal born children of Kinfolk would probably be excluded from much of the social life in neighborhoods or villages of Kinfolk and would probably be encouraged to leave as soon as they reach adulthood). In the second case, the mundane Kinfolk would know that they are descended from a supernatural heritage of werewolves that guide and protect the members of their family from supernatural enemies that wish to do them harm and would honor Gaia, the Celestines, and the Incarna. In the third case, the magical Kinfolk and the Garou know as much as any other member of their Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T18:20:31-07:00","id":1102165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1102132#post1102132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a gene. No matter how much KABA went backsliding on a rocket sled, it simply just doesn't make sense in terms of polypeptide chains. Hence DNA's terminal confusion at their results.<br /> <br /> (Also, it being recessive double doesn't make sense, because recessive traits often get to be the way they are because production of a polypeptide chain either got turned off completely or ended up as nonfunctional. Also, it keeps things too basic in an explanation of genetics, since it ignores complex traits, penetrance, and other factors not covered in introductory life science sections.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but we're dealing with something which is not entirely magical OR entirely genetic so we have to deal with it. There's a biological element to being Garou as well as a spiritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T21:30:20-07:00","id":1102186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1102165#post1102165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but we're dealing with something which is not entirely magical OR entirely genetic so we have to deal with it. There's a biological element to being Garou as well as a spiritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>A biological element that somehow never shows up on biological texts. Ever.<br /> <br /> (Revised did much good in killing the concept of the Garou gene. I lament said concept's return.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T22:53:32-07:00","id":1102203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1102186#post1102186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A biological element that somehow never shows up on biological texts. Ever.<br /> <br /> (Revised did much good in killing the concept of the Garou gene. I lament said concept's return.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the same for vampires, ghouls, and all the other biological supernaturals. And science is controlled by the Illuminati, preventing scientists from discovering the world's cryptids. You've got to accept some breaks from reality to play the premise.<br /> <br /> Saying, &quot;garou biology is wholly supernatural&quot; is irksome to me because it removes a lot of the game's grounding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T23:13:13-07:00","id":1102204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1102203#post1102203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the same for vampires, ghouls, and all the other biological supernaturals. And science is controlled by the Illuminati, preventing scientists from discovering the world's cryptids. You've got to accept some breaks from reality to play the premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Mage's problem, and it's welcome to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Saying, &quot;garou biology is wholly supernatural&quot; is irksome to me because it removes a lot of the game's grounding. </div> </div> </div>It describes it as being the result of a fusion of spirit and flesh. Which no wholly physical test will trip off. Because, quite frankly, there's not much of a way to explain whatever Garou and Fera do without going heavy on supernatural explanations, or in their case I supposed you could say ultranatural explanations, because even if you can eventually explain a process of shapeshifting that wholly conforms to physics and biology, it wouldn't be the shapeshifting of changers or include any of the benefits of the state of being a changer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T05:10:29-07:00","id":1102236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1102186#post1102186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A biological element that somehow never shows up on biological texts. Ever.<br /> <br /> (Revised did much good in killing the concept of the Garou gene. I lament said concept's return.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think it should be something that can be found... with appropriate Spheres, Paths, or other supernatural methods. Not so much on a standard paternity test.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T06:37:34-07:00","id":1102250,"title":"","content":"Transformation of ephemera into living matter (and visa versa) is a nice pseudo-scientific explanation for the biology of the Garou. It explains the regeneration and the shapeshifting. I honestly think that MtAs is much more difficult to explain through the internal logic of cWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T09:55:46-07:00","id":1102289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101722-is-the-birth-rate-of-garou-mathematically-impossible?p=1101950#post1101950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression from the books as well as my experience from gameplay is that the majority of non-SF Garou are born to Kin-Kin pairings who are not directly connected to Garou society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I rarely have seen the tribebooks and such actually discuss the issue of having cubs pop up randomly. GW book had it, but the rest generally seem to assume the cub either grew up in the family or knows at least something.<br /> <br /> Add to it every houserule how people see lost cubs, and you got a mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T10:29:51-07:00","id":1102293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote